      "assessment": "R5 G4 gives a coherent branch-local history and correctly labels inherited clipping evidence. It proposes a restoration and a joint comparator pair isolating the early level between those two proposals. It still describes its private best as globally best, overlooking the peer, and the direction of some Best/top10 claims is inconsistent with its own values.",
      "decision_update": "Only [6,6,4,6] enters the final archived ranking; [5,6,4,6] is rejected. No sampling follows. The paired-proposal concept is useful, but selecting only one member removes the proposed same-wave discrimination, so its evidence value must be recalculated.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "A historical mean deficit to mixed TOP1 is not a causal control. The teacher score is not an affinity ceiling; the concentration and small delivered displacement do not establish which untested schedule would improve.",
