      "assessment": "R5 council explicitly respects zero remaining rounds and labels the final choices unexecuted, while recognising branch-local r labels. It still propagates the false99-pair claim, calls a real concentrated loss non-directional, and includes R0 among a list described as nominally tied despite the 0.054 gap. Its selected G4:H1 Best/top10 are actually below that branch latest, contrary to the reason.",
      "decision_update": "Final archive ranks [6,6,4,6], [6,6,5,5], [6,6,6,5], [6,5,5,5]; no R6 is launched. V2’s actual R5 best-Mean group is [6,6,4,5], Mean4.123637, while best individual score belongs to another group. The review must use executed results, not these future suggestions.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The version retains about the same Top2 TOP1 Mean asV1 but does not improve fixed-group Mean. More polished, longer rationales have not demonstrated higher search efficiency. Generic revisions require evidence-led comparison identity, contributor accounting and marginal information value, not transfer of the observed winning arrays.",
